1.1.text:
CHAPTER III

RESPONSIBILITY

Article 4

1. The Regional Government is responsible for implementing efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence in the form of:a. Collecting data and information about women and children victims of violence in accordance with Laws and Regulations;

www.jdih.manggaraibaratkab.go.id
b. Conducting education on anti-violence values against women and children;
c. Disseminating Laws and Regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
d. Conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of services and protection for women and children victims of violence;
2. To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government provides and organizes services for victims in the form: a. Establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims involving community elements; b. Encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for victims.
3. The Regional Government in providing and organizing services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must consider the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The Principles of Services and Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence are:

a. Respect and recognition of equal and equivalent human rights and dignity;
b. Respect for the rights of victims;
c. Justice and gender equality;
d. Non-discriminatory; ande. Best interests of the victim.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

REGENT OF WEST MANGGARAI,

Considering:
a.
b. c. that violence and discrimination in any form against women and children constitutes a violation of Human Rights, therefore violence and discrimination against women and children occurring in West Manggarai Regency must receive optimal services and protection;

that the provision of services for women victims of violence and child protection is one of the authorities of the regency government in accordance with the provisions of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, therefore it needs to be regulated by Regional Regulation;

that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Services and Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

www.jdih.manggaraibaratkab.go.id In View of:
1. 2.

3.

Article 8

1. The forms of services and protection for victims organized by P3A consist of: www.jdih.manggaraibaratkab.go.id
a. Medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical injuries aimed at restoring the physical condition of victims carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. Medicolegal services are a form of medical services for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
c. Psychosocial services are services provided by assistants in order to restore the traumatic condition of victims, including the provision of safe houses to protect victims from various threats and intimidation for victims and to provide social support so that victims have self-confidence, strength and independence in resolving their problems;
d. Legal services to assist victims in undergoing the judicial process;
e. Economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and providing economic access so that victims can be independent.
2. Further provisions regarding the mechanism of services and protection as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be organized according to Standard Operational Procedures (SOP) which will be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

